.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Bardeen, Cooper, and Schrieffer explained superconductivity as a condensate of Cooper pairs bound by an effective attraction, however weak. Pairing opens a gap \Delta in the single-particle excitation spectrum: unlike the normal-state band |\xi(k)|, which touches zero at the Fermi points, the BCS quasiparticle band E(k) = \sqrt{\xi(k)^2 + |\Delta(k)|^2} never does. bdg_bcs_hamiltonian builds the Bogoliubov-de Gennes Hamiltonian in Nambu (particle-hole) space, and bdg_spectrum diagonalizes it across the Brillouin zone.">

